# Board defaults for nvidia-generic.
#
# Inherits everything from amd64-generic (see profiles/base/parent); this file only
# states what differs.

# Mesa drivers to build. The iGPU path (amdgpu/radeonsi) is kept because it is the
# recovery console and must always work -- Stage 2 deliberately keeps the display on
# the iGPU while the NVIDIA driver is brought up.
#
# nouveau is included as a *diagnostic* fallback, not the intended driver. If the
# NVIDIA module misbehaves it lets us prove PCI enumeration, DRM/KMS and modesetting
# independently. minigbm already ships a nouveau dumb-buffer backend, so this path
# works without patches, which makes it a useful control experiment.
VIDEO_CARDS="amdgpu radeonsi nouveau"

# Pull the NVIDIA stack into the image via the board BSP package.
USE="${USE} nvidia_open"
